# ===========================================================================
# EAS ONLY. Everything ABOVE this banner is a verbatim copy of .gitignore.
#
# .easignore REPLACES .gitignore for eas-cli, it does not add to it. From the
# moment this file exists no .gitignore anywhere in the tree is read; only
# `.git` and `node_modules` stay hardcoded. A .easignore holding just the rule
# below would therefore stop applying every protective rule above it: .env,
# android/, dist/, .expo/ and the *.jks / *.p8 / *.p12 / *.mobileprovision
# patterns. On the default GitClient path the archive is a clone of the TRACKED
# tree, so an untracked .env could not leak that way -- but under EAS_NO_VCS=1
# (or a non-git checkout) eas-cli walks the WORKING COPY filtered by this file
# alone, and then it would.
#
# Regenerate, never hand-edit the copied part:
#   cp .gitignore .easignore
# then re-append this block. __tests__/lib/easignore.test.ts fails on any drift
# between the two files, and on any second rule appearing down here.
#
# NEVER add a rule matching anything under assets/. The build backend writes
# assets/images/{icon,splash-icon}.png (ProcessBuildTask::injectAssets) and
# assets/t/ (AssetPackStager) into its clone AFTER cloning and BEFORE
# `eas build`. Excluding assets/images/ fails the worker ~20 minutes in with
# `resource drawable/splashscreen_logo not found`; excluding assets/t/ breaks
# Metro, because the rule is path-based and drops the artwork COMMITTED in the
# repo alongside the staged pack, leaving the literal require('@/assets/t/...')
# calls in constants/t/asset-slots.ts with nothing to resolve.
#
# Pack SOURCES, on the other hand, are pure build input: nothing requires them,
# so they are bundled by nothing and only ever travelled to EAS as dead weight.
# ===========================================================================
asset-packs/
